{
 "schema": "m8_layer_a_capture_provenance.v1",
 "book": "Ezek",
 "lane": "ezek_primaries",
 "law": "OW-18",
 "built_at": "2026-09-15T21:36:39.924846+00:00",
 "what_this_is": "the evidence tier of the OW-7 Layer A record for every landed Ezekiel primary execution. It exists because 30 packets landed before the landing tool required a capture-carrier field, and a silent record asserts by its identical shape that nothing changed about how it was produced.",
 "how_the_tier_was_decided": "MEASURED, not remembered. For each execution the harness transcript was stat-ed by exact path, its final assistant message re-extracted, and the resulting JSON compared field-by-field against the landed record with the orchestrator's own note set aside. EXTRACTED means the landed record is still re-derivable from a durable artifact today. TRANSCRIBED means it is not, because the transcript is absent or 0 bytes, so the record's only carrier was the completion notification in the orchestrator's context.",
 "honest_limits": [
  "This measures re-derivability TODAY, which is a stronger and different claim than what happened at land time. A record could have been extracted at land time from a transcript that was later truncated; such a record reads TRANSCRIBED here. The tier is therefore conservative: it never over-claims, and it may under-claim.",
  "The orchestrator's belief about its own past procedure is deliberately NOT used as evidence anywhere in this file.",
  "A tier says nothing about the scholarly quality of the review it carries. A TRANSCRIBED record's findings are neither better nor worse; only their chain of custody is weaker.",
  "The two TRANSCRIBED records each additionally carry a MEASURED deliverable digest equal to the transcribed one, and the landing tool verified record-to-deliverable parity over rows_reviewed and the recomputed tally. That corroboration is real and it does NOT upgrade the tier."
 ],
 "counts_by_tier": {
